{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1789"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c150): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c150.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1789"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge music-stage/pop-rock","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/music-stage__pop-rock.g3.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",552],["+","In between came „Animals“ in January 1977, whose cover shoot produced one of rock's strangest news stories. "],["=",2],["+","3 December 1976 a 40-foot inflatable pig was tethered above Battersea Power Station in London; it broke loose, drifted into the flight paths of Heathrow, where air traffic was brought to a standstill for a while, and finally came down on a farm in Kent. The pig, later named Algie, became Pink Floyd's mascot and a fixture of their concerts. The band's last album, „The Endless River“ of November 2014, built from leftover session recordings, even features a scientist: on the track „Talkin' Hawkin'“ Stephen Hawking speaks with his synthesised voice, sampled from a British Telecom advertisement that the band had already used on „Keep Talking“ in 1994.\n\nOn "],["=",455]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",526],["+","Dazwischen erschien im Januar 1977 „Animals“, dessen Covershooting eine der seltsamsten Meldungen der Rockgeschichte lieferte. "],["=",2],["+","3. Dezember 1976 wurde über der Battersea Power Station in London ein zwölf Meter langes aufblasbares Schwein festgemacht; es riss sich los, trieb in die Einflugschneisen von Heathrow, wo der Flugverkehr eine Zeit lang zum Erliegen kam, und landete schließlich auf einem Bauernhof in Kent. Das Schwein, später Algie getauft, wurde zum Maskottchen von Pink Floyd und zum festen Bestandteil ihrer Konzerte. Das letzte Album der Band, „The Endless River“ vom November 2014, aus übrig gebliebenen Session-Aufnahmen gebaut, hat sogar einen Wissenschaftler zu Gast: Im Stück „Talkin' Hawkin'“ spricht Stephen Hawking mit seiner Synthesizerstimme, entnommen einem Werbespot von British Telecom, den die Band schon 1994 für „Keep Talking“ verwendet hatte.\n\nAm "],["=",437]]}]},
